# LeakSanitizer suppressions for scripts/leak-check.sh.
#
# Each line hides every leak whose allocation stack passes through a frame
# matching it, at any depth. A broad one -- a whole library, or anything
# the event loop calls -- would hide our own leaks too, since everything in
# the shim runs under Qt's event loop. So only functions that never call
# back into our code belong here, each with the reason it is there.
#
# Taken from piirit's, which measured them on the same Qt 5.15 (Ubuntu's)
# across its whole suite; kept only as long as vuo's run still needs them.

# The offscreen platform plugin makes its QScreen, QPlatformScreen and
# cursor at startup and never deletes them; they point at each other, so
# LeakSanitizer sees a cycle nothing reaches. Qt's own, once per process,
# and only on the offscreen platform the tests run on.
leak:QGuiApplicationPrivate::createPlatformIntegration

# Connections QML makes to that same screen -- the `Screen` attached
# property, and the window watching its screen -- which live in the
# leaked screen's connection list and so are reported with it.
leak:QQuickScreenInfo::setWrappedScreen
leak:QQuickWindowPrivate::init
